{"name":"Land of Nod","hex":"#a99b88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"land","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of Earth which is not covered by oceans or other bodies of water.","Real estate or landed property; a partitioned and measurable area which is owned and acquired and on which buildings and structures can be built and erected."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To descend to a surface, especially from the air.","To alight, to descend from a vehicle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land"},{"term":"nod","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Northern Thai."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To incline the head up and down, as to indicate agreement.","To briefly incline the head downwards as a cursory greeting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nod"}],"entries":[{"title":"Land of Nod","blocks":[{"text":"The Land of Nod is a place mentioned in the Book of Genesis of the Hebrew Bible, located \"on the east of Eden\" (qiḏmaṯ-ʿḖḏen), where Cain was exiled by God after Cain had murdered his brother Abel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Thomas_Stackhouse%2C_The_place_of_Paradise%2C_the_habitation_of_Adam_and_Seth%2C_and_the_Land_of_Nod_%28FL50795203_2369068%29.jpg/330px-Thomas_Stackhouse%2C_The_place_of_Paradise%2C_the_habitation_of_Adam_and_Seth%2C_and_the_Land_of_Nod_%28FL50795203_2369068%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_of_Nod","wikidata":"Q1929769"},{"title":"Land","blocks":[{"text":"Land, also known as dry land, ground, or earth, is the solid terrestrial surface of Earth not submerged by the ocean or another body of water. It makes up approximately 29% of Earth's surface and includes all continents and islands. Earth's land surface is almost entirely covered by regolith, a layer of rock, soil, and minerals that forms the outer part of the crust. Land plays an important role in Earth's climate system, being involved in the carbon cycle, nitrogen cycle, and water cycle. One-third of land is covered in trees another third is used for agriculture, and roughly one-tenth is covered in glacier ice. The remainder consists of desert, savannah, and prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg/330px-Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land","wikidata":"Q11081619"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah%27s_Curse.jpg/500px-Cormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah%27s_Curse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah%27s_Curse.jpg/1280px-Cormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah%27s_Curse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah%27s_Curse.jpg/500px-Cormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah%27s_Curse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Cain fleeing before Jehovah's Curse, by Fernand-Anne Piestre Cormon, c. 1880","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACormon%2C_Fernand_-_Cain_flying_before_Jehovah's_Curse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Gateway_to_%22Land_of_Nod%22_on_Grayshott_Road_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1705069.jpg/500px-Gateway_to_%22Land_of_Nod%22_on_Grayshott_Road_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1705069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://